  "releaseNotes": "JsonSchemaConverter/SelfReferencingJsonSchemaConverter now populate Enum for enum-typed properties and root types (previously a bare untyped \"string\") — an explicit per-member System.Text.Json JsonStringEnumMemberNameAttribute or Newtonsoft/DataAnnotations EnumMemberAttribute always wins, falling back to the new overridable EnumNamingPolicy for everything else. IsRequired now also recognizes the C# `required` member modifier. GetJsonPropertyName, IsRequired, and ApplyValidationAttributes on JsonSchemaConverterBase are now protected virtual (previously static), joining GetJsonSchemaType/GetJsonSchemaFormat as full extension points for a derived converter — see Package.md for the extensibility contract.",
